The exact script \path{code/III/manifolds_star_log_caps.py}
retains the twelve actual canonical bases,
the full normalization matrices, the
literal fibre and normal maps, and their
complete integral kernels. It checks
the conductor calculation independently
against the mapping-torus sequence and
compares the global Smith formula on
unbounded symbolic lattices and a finite
set of exact instances. The proof above,
including the order-two marking, is
independent of the finite parameter
bounds used in those corroborating runs.
Root actions with nonprimitive gamma
power, other integral star blocks and
positive-weight star degenerations are
outside this theorem's stated scope.
